Template: rustyrig-server/admin-password
Type: password
Default:
Description: Password for the RustyRig admin account:
 Choose the password used to log in as the RustyRig admin user.  This is
 required when creating a new server database.  An existing database is not
 changed during upgrades.

Template: rustyrig-server/enable-guest
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Enable the shared guest account?
 The shipped guest permissions allow receive audio and chat only. You must
 choose a separate guest password if enabling this account. Enable this if you want
 shared guest access to your LAN/VPN station.
 .
 The account is disabled by default. This choice applies only when creating
 a new server database; existing accounts are preserved during upgrades.

Template: rustyrig/admin-users
Type: string
Default:
Description: Local users to add to the rradmin group:
 Enter existing local usernames separated by spaces. Members can read,
 modify and delete RustyRig logs and maintain its SQLite databases.
 Leave empty to add nobody. Existing group members are retained.
 Users must log in again after being added to the group.

Template: rustyrig/serial-users
Type: string
Default:
Description: Local users to add to the rruser device-access group:
 Enter existing local usernames separated by spaces. Members can open
 RustyRig virtual serial ports (including CAT and GPS) created by rrclient.
 This is separate from rradmin and does not grant administrative permissions.
 Leave empty to add nobody. Existing memberships are preserved.
 Members must log out and back in for new group access.

Template: rustyrig-server/allow-remote-admin
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Allow selected users from linked RustyRig servers to administer this server?
 Default is no. This grants privileged remote administration only to
 explicitly listed authenticated user@site identities after their origin
 server has been securely enrolled and verified. It does not enroll or trust
 a server certificate. This applies only to a new database.

Template: rustyrig-server/remote-admin-subjects
Type: string
Default:
Description: Remote administrator identities (user@site, space separated):
 Enter one or more usernames qualified by the authoritative RustyRig site
 name, such as alice@camp. A user need not exist yet: access is effective
 only after authentication through a trusted, pinned mesh identity.
 .
 user@* grants that username access from ANY authenticated remote site and
 is substantially broader. Prefer explicit user@site identities. No other
 users receive remote privileges by default.

Template: rustyrig-server/guest-password
Type: password
Default:
Description: Password for the optional RustyRig guest account:
 Required when the guest account is enabled. Never use a shared default
 password; choose a distinct secret and distribute it only to intended users.

Template: rustyrig-server/site-domain
Type: string
Default:
Description: RustyRig mesh domain:
 Enter the shared mesh domain (for example, ham.example.net).
 All servers in a mesh must use the same domain.
 Leave empty to retain the existing setting.

Template: rustyrig-server/site-name
Type: string
Default:
Description: RustyRig node name:
 Enter the unique station name within the mesh (for example, dsmiia00).
 The full node identity is station.name.domain.
 Leave empty to retain the existing setting.
 Changing an enrolled node identity may require certificate and peer updates.

Template: rustyrig-server/site-call
Type: string
Default:
Description: Station callsign:
 Enter the public callsign for this station (for example, N0CALL/P).
 Leave empty to retain the existing setting.

Template: rustyrig-server/site-grid
Type: string
Default:
Description: Station Maidenhead grid square:
 Enter the station locator (for example, EN31eo).
 Leave empty to retain the existing setting.

Template: rustyrig-server/site-location
Type: string
Default:
Description: Station location:
 Enter the public station location, such as City, State, Country, or MOBILE.
 Leave empty to retain the existing setting.

Template: rustyrig-server/site-description
Type: string
Default:
Description: Station description:
 Enter a short public description of the station or receiver.
 Leave empty to retain the existing setting.

Template: rustyrig-server/site-pending
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Pending station metadata update (internal)
 This flag preserves answers between configuration and package installation.
